<p><a id=3D"raw-section-8"></a></p>
<h3>A realistic production budget</h3>
<p>An early R episode might need 45 minutes of idea work, 45 minutes of out=
lining, 30 minutes of setup/practice, 45 minutes of recording, 90 minutes o=
f editing, 30 minutes of packaging, and 30 minutes of upload checks. That i=
s <strong>315 minutes, or 5 hours 15 minutes</strong>, before additional re=
search and audience review. Beginners may need more. The fortnightly schedu=
le deliberately leaves room for learning and documenting experiments.</p>
<p>The quality gate is simple: a clear promise, an honest example, intellig=
ible audio, a coherent middle, and an action the viewer can take. Publish a=
 modest complete lesson when those conditions hold. Do not postpone it for =
decorative effects.</p>
