<p><a id=3D"sample-scripts"></a></p>
<h2>Original scripts you can adapt</h2>
<p>These are original teaching samples. They are not transcriptions or imit=
ations of either creator. The first can be filmed as a demonstration today;=
 it makes no claim that you completed a past transformation. Keep only stat=
ements that match your beliefs and situation.</p>
<p><a id=3D"sample-scripts-section-1"></a></p>
<h3>R sample: Before you start another course, choose one thing to finish</=
h3>
<p><strong>Spoken draft =E2=80=94 roughly a four-minute starting point; tim=
e your own read.</strong></p>
<p>If you keep starting courses but cannot name what you have finished, try=
 making one decision before your next lesson: what will exist when you are =
done?</p>
<p>I don=E2=80=99t mean that every book or video needs to become a side hus=
tle. Learning for its own sake can be enjoyable. I mean the situation where=
 you want a practical skill, keep collecting resources, and still do not kn=
ow what to do with them.</p>
<p>Here is an example. =E2=80=9CLearn web development=E2=80=9D sounds like =
a plan, but it leaves a lot undecided. What are you going to build? How muc=
h is enough? When you sit down tonight, what do you actually open?</p>
<p>Compare that with: =E2=80=9CMake one page that explains a topic I unders=
tand.=E2=80=9D It does not need accounts, payments, or an impressive design=
. It needs a heading, an explanation, and a way for someone to read it.</p>
<p>[Show a page with those three requirements.]</p>
<p>Now the learning has a job. If you do not know how to put a heading on a=
 page, find that lesson. If you do not know how to publish it, learn that s=
tep. You can still explore later. But tonight you have a reason to choose o=
ne piece of information instead of collecting ten possibilities.</p>
<p>You can use this outside coding too. If you are learning to draw, your o=
utput could be three attempts at the same object. If you are learning to ex=
plain an idea, record a two-minute explanation. The important part is makin=
g the finish line visible enough that you can recognize it.</p>
<p>I would do this in three steps.</p>
<p>First, name the smallest useful output. Make it smaller than the version=
 you would like to show off. =E2=80=9CA draft someone can understand=E2=80=
=9D is a finish line. =E2=80=9CSomething impressive=E2=80=9D is a moving ta=
rget.</p>
<p>Second, write the next action. =E2=80=9CWork on the project=E2=80=9D is =
still vague. =E2=80=9CWrite the first paragraph=E2=80=9D tells you what to =
do when you sit down. If the action needs several decisions before you can =
begin, make it more specific.</p>
<p>Third, stop and review when that small output exists. Ask what you can n=
ow do, where you got stuck, and what you need next. That review gives your =
next lesson a purpose.</p>
<p>[Show a card: Output. Next action. Review.]</p>
<p>There is a trap here. You can spend so long designing the perfect projec=
t that planning becomes another form of collecting. Give yourself a short d=
ecision window. Choose something small enough that the first attempt can be=
 rough.</p>
<p>This will not solve every reason someone struggles to start. Sometimes t=
he task is genuinely difficult. Sometimes there is not enough time, or anot=
her problem deserves attention first. The point is simply to remove one avo=
idable decision: what am I trying to make?</p>
<p>Before your next study session, write this sentence: =E2=80=9CWhen I fin=
ish, I will have=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D Then describe one thing you could show s=
omeone. Under it, write the first action you can take tonight.</p>
<p>You do not need a new system to try it. One page is enough. Use the next=
 lesson to help you make the thing you chose.</p>
<p><strong>Edit map:</strong> camera for the opening; notebook at the vague=
/specific comparison; camera through the three steps; one short three-part =
card; camera for the limitation; notebook for the final sentence. No music =
is required. Add a relevant next-video link only if that video actually exi=
sts.</p>
